Changes made by this project to the baseline (see docs/PORT-SPEC.md):

  1. The architecture identity macro (NINFER_SM86 / NINFER_SM89) is
     defined at directory scope from CMAKE_CUDA_ARCHITECTURES in the
     top-level CMakeLists.txt; the hard-coded NINFER_SM86=1 target
     definition in src/CMakeLists.txt is removed.
  2. Every NINFER_SM86 preprocessor conditional in the tree also
     accepts NINFER_SM89 (behaviour-preserving: Ada already took the
     compatibility branch under the Ampere name).
  3. src/core/device.h / device.cu: device_sm_count() - the runtime
     streaming-multiprocessor count of the device this process runs
     on, queried once and cached.
  4. src/ops/linear_attention/gated_delta_net/chunked/output.cu: the
     resident-wave target is derived from device_sm_count() instead
     of a hard-coded RTX 5090 SM count (the kernel runs on 49 of the
     65 Qwen3.8-27B layers).
  5. src/ops/sparse_moe/prefill/sparse_moe_prefill_kernels.cu: the
     prefill grid cap is derived from device_sm_count() instead of a
     hard-coded RTX 5090 SM count (Qwen3.6-35B-A3B path only).
  6. src/ops/gdn_gating_proj/bf16/bf16_gdn_gating_proj_kernels.cu:
     the cooperative-residency constant for Bf16Gdn27Geometry is
     split-aware (split-8 -> 2 CTAs/SM, split-4/2 -> 1). On a part
     with fewer SMs than the RTX 4090 the old constant made the
     driver reject the launch with cudaErrorCooperativeLaunchTooLarge.

The upstream sources are not redistributed in this repository; the
port is applied to a fresh clone of the baseline by the tooling in
tools/ and scripts/.
